(6963944, 1049236, 62787, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jaysonmc:</b></div><hr/><i> The angle and color on this is stunning.<br/> <br/>Hope you returned to DPC? Good to see familiar names. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks :) And yes - hope to finally be around more often again! Got swallowed for a while by my PhD, but now that I''ve emerged on the other side, I actually have time for photography again.</td>', 'Originally posted by jaysonmc: The angle and color on this is stunning. Hope you returned to DPC? Good to see familiar names.   Thanks :) And yes - hope to finally be around more often again! Got swallowed for a while by my PhD, but now that I''ve emerged on the other side, I actually have time for photography again.', '2013-01-24 18:34:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6964110, 1049117, 18197, '<td valign="top">Max, great score for this. Well done. Keep it up! Go Elysium!!!!!!</td>', 'Max, great score for this. Well done. Keep it up! Go Elysium!!!!!!', '2013-01-25 01:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6964774, 1049297, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by frisca:</b></div><hr/><i> you know what I especially like about this image? It has an impressionist quality about it, without being obvious. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>What do you mean? Mentioning Dégas was a blasphemy??</td>', 'Originally posted by frisca: you know what I especially like about this image? It has an impressionist quality about it, without being obvious.  What do you mean? Mentioning Dégas was a blasphemy??', '2013-01-26 04:23:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6965534, 1049030, 66952, '<td valign="top">Ahh...one of those images that finishes somewhere in the middle, but nobody gives you a clue what went wrong. I hate that when that happens. As far as the image itself, the lighting is good, you''ve given a very good view of the textures. I think why it finished somewhere in the middle on the challenge was the subject matter. Pictures sculpture just don''t do that well.</td>', 'Ahh...one of those images that finishes somewhere in the middle, but nobody gives you a clue what went wrong. I hate that when that happens. As far as the image itself, the lighting is good, you''ve given a very good view of the textures. I think why it finished somewhere in the middle on the challenge was the subject matter. Pictures sculpture just don''t do that well.', '2013-01-27 19:11:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6965557, 1049030, 138630, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=66952" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Ann</a> picked up on the two things that impressed me - lighting and textures.  Nice.</td>', ' Ann picked up on the two things that impressed me - lighting and textures.  Nice.', '2013-01-27 20:13:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(6965595, 1049030, 136989, '<td valign="top">The lighting is terrific.  B/w was a good choice here to show the textures.  The subject itself didn''t capture my attention though.</td>', 'The lighting is terrific.  B/w was a good choice here to show the textures.  The subject itself didn''t capture my attention though.', '2013-01-27 22:05:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6965896, 1049297, 96530, '<td valign="top">I didn''t get around to commenting on this one while it was still on the front page. But this is perhaps my favorite image done by you for DPC Wendy, really nice work!</td>', 'I didn''t get around to commenting on this one while it was still on the front page. But this is perhaps my favorite image done by you for DPC Wendy, really nice work!', '2013-01-28 13:07:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6966387, 1049030, 75713, '<td valign="top">Your photo is one of the reasons I like side challenges much more that challenges.  It seems in challenges everyone has a preconceived notion of what is an acceptable entry to meet their perception of an often time poorly written description of what the challenge is - descriptions can never connect with all the participants as we come from so many different cultures, belief systems and even though, on the surface, we might come from the same country, town and the like, our interpretations are based on our life''s view and roughly one second of viewing and then on to the rest quickly quickly.  <br/>It''s true as Ann wrote that sculptures don''t so well - but that is where side challenges come into their best - When I look at what you have presented I enlarge the photo so that the stand is not in my view. It then becomes something else - a study in texture and light - it''s almost completed face is recognizable as a horse waiting patiently for it''s ears.  One of the most powerful anatomical parts of a horse are it''s powerful legs and the lack of legs makes me wonder what the creator is trying to convey .. even it''s tail, usually such a finishing touch to the magnificent appearance of a horse is clumped into a shape that conveys no motion - I find it all fascinating once I stop viewing it as a finished sculpture. As for your quest to light it properly, in my eyes, you excelled.</td>', 'Your photo is one of the reasons I like side challenges much more that challenges.  It seems in challenges everyone has a preconceived notion of what is an acceptable entry to meet their perception of an often time poorly written description of what the challenge is - descriptions can never connect with all the participants as we come from so many different cultures, belief systems and even though, on the surface, we might come from the same country, town and the like, our interpretations are based on our life''s view and roughly one second of viewing and then on to the rest quickly quickly.  It''s true as Ann wrote that sculptures don''t so well - but that is where side challenges come into their best - When I look at what you have presented I enlarge the photo so that the stand is not in my view. It then becomes something else - a study in texture and light - it''s almost completed face is recognizable as a horse waiting patiently for it''s ears.  One of the most powerful anatomical parts of a horse are it''s powerful legs and the lack of legs makes me wonder what the creator is trying to convey .. even it''s tail, usually such a finishing touch to the magnificent appearance of a horse is clumped into a shape that conveys no motion - I find it all fascinating once I stop viewing it as a finished sculpture. As for your quest to light it properly, in my eyes, you excelled.', '2013-01-29 14:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(6969160, 1049030, 5112, '<td valign="top">Nice, even light.  How that horse stays balanced on that block is a mystery!</td>', 'Nice, even light.  How that horse stays balanced on that block is a mystery!', '2013-02-01 14:02:58.000000', NULL, 0),
